  "equipment_type": "Split air conditioner BACnet gateway (1 indoor unit)",
  "applies_to": "Panasonic Etherea and other residential (RAC) split indoor units with a CN-CNT connector.",
  "summary": "One-unit Intesis interface that plugs into the CN-CNT socket of a Panasonic residential indoor unit and exposes it on BACnet MS/TP as 47 objects. Besides on/off, mode, setpoint, fan and vane control it covers power use and accumulated energy, Powerful and Quiet modes, room freeze protection, ECONAVI/AutoComfort, the human-activity sensor, nanoe X / nanoe-G, occupancy logic and a virtual-temperature function.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 246000,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names follow the manual's object summary table. The detailed object pages spell a few differently (SetPoint_command, nanoeX_status, nanoeX_command, nanoe-G_status, nanoe-G_command, the occupancy setpoints with 'SetPoint', UnoccupiedDeadbandAction).",
    "The summary table lists AccumulatedEnergy as BV 5, but its object page shows Analog Value 5 in Wh; it is listed here as AV 5.",
    "The EcoMode_command object page shows the identifier as Multistate Output 0; the summary table gives MO 4, which is used here (MO 0 is Mode_command).",
    "Which functions work (Powerful, Quiet, ECONAVI, nanoe, freeze protection, vanes) depends on the indoor unit model. SW1 P1 sets whether the unit has a fan-only mode and SW1 P2 whether it has horizontal vanes.",
    "Temperature units follow the °C/°F DIP switch (SW2 position 8)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "IN485PAN001I000 Gateway - Panasonic Etherea/RAC Systems to BACnet MS/TP - User Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "2024-09-17 v1.0.6",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user_manual_in485pan001i000.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Plug the gateway into the CN-CNT socket of the indoor unit, set the MS/TP MAC address and baud rate on the DIP switches, then write the _command objects (on/off, mode, setpoint, fan, vanes) and read the matching _status objects. One gateway serves one indoor unit.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 0",
        "name": "OnOff_command",
        "why": "Start/stop the indoor unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 0",
        "name": "Mode_command",
        "why": "Heat/cool/fan/dry/auto selection"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 0",
        "name": "Setpoint_command",
        "why": "Temperature setpoint from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 1",
        "name": "FanSpeed_command",
        "why": "Fan speed selection"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 0",
        "name": "OnOff_status",
        "why": "Confirm the unit is running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "SetPoint_status",
        "why": "Setpoint the unit is really using"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "RoomTemperature_status",
        "why": "Room/return temperature for trending"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1",
        "name": "ErrorActive",
        "why": "Unit alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "ErrorCode",
        "why": "Which fault is active"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No enable point is documented; the gateway accepts commands as soon as it talks to the unit. BV 2 LockRemoteControl can lock out the wired remote.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "Write the BMS room temperature to AO 1 RoomTemperature_command and the setpoint to AO 0 Setpoint_command. The gateway then runs its Virtual Temperature function and recalculates the setpoint it sends to the unit; BI 14 VirtualTempActive shows it is active and AI 17 UserSetPoint_status shows the BMS setpoint.",
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance 246000; in automatic mode it is 246000 + the MS/TP MAC address set on DIP switch SW2 (P1-P7).",
      "Writing Object_Identifier from BACnet switches the gateway to manual addressing until a factory reset.",
      "SW1 P6-P8 set the baud rate (autobaud by default); SW1 P1-P2 describe the unit (fan mode, horizontal vanes).",
      "SW3 enables the 120-ohm terminator and bus biasing."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Write the _command object and read the _status object; they share instance numbers in different object types.",
      "The Occupancy MV and its four setpoint AVs drive built-in logic; leave Occupancy at 3 (Disabled) if the BMS handles scheduling.",
      "PowerConsumption (AI 3) rolls over at 65535 W."
    ]
  },
  "covers_brands": [
